    moodNeutralAbove: 33
  texts:
    stepNames:
    - Charge
    - Prosecution
    - Defense
    - Friend
    - Verdict
    - Plan
    worryName: The Worry
    prosecutorName: The Prosecutor
    prosecutorLine: Your Honor, look at all this evidence. The worry is clearly
      true!
    defenderName: The Defender
    defenderLine: Objection! Let us put the facts on the other side of the scale.
    friendName: The Friend
    friendLine: If I were your friend, here is what I would say to you.
    judgeName: The Judge
    judgeLine: The court will now give its verdict.
    clerkName: The Clerk
    clerkLine: 'One last thing: what small step will you take?'
    worryFarewell: ...I was only a thought, after all.
    meterFormat: WORRY LEVEL  {value}%
    introHeading: 'Today''s case: {case}'
    introLead: You are the judge. A worry has been brought to court. Weigh the evidence
      for and against it, hear what a friend would say, and give a verdict.
    introButton: Open the trial
    sortHeading: 'Prosecution: evidence for the worry'
    sortLead: Is this a fact the court can check, or a feeling or a guess? Only facts
      are admitted.
    evidenceCounter: EVIDENCE {n} OF {total}
    factButton: Fact
    guessButton: Feeling or guess
    factAdmitted: Admitted. This is a fact. It can be checked.
    guessNotAdmitted: Not admitted. This is {trap}. {description}
    wrongSaidGuess: Look again. You could check this one, so it counts as a fact.
    wrongSaidFact: Look again. Nobody can check this one. It is a thought or a feeling.
    nextEvidenceButton: Next evidence
    toDefenceButton: On to the defense
    defenceHeading: 'Defense: evidence against the worry'
    defenceLead: 'Pick {needed} facts that show the worry might not be true. Admitted:
      {picked} of {needed}.'
    defenceAdmitted: Admitted. This is a real fact that weighs against the worry.
    toFriendButton: Call the Friend
    friendHeading: The Friend takes the stand
    friendPrompt: A friend has the same worry and asks for advice. What would you
      tell them?
    friendCorrect: Kind and realistic. You'd say this to a friend, and you can say
      it to yourself.
    toVerdictButton: To the verdict
    verdictHeading: The Verdict
    verdictPrompt: Pick the more balanced and helpful thought you can believe instead.
    verdictCorrect: Balanced and believable. The court no longer accepts the worry as a fact.
    toPlanButton: Make a plan
    planHeading: The Plan
    planPrompt: Choose one small action that supports the new thought, then say when
      you'll do it.
    planCorrect: Small, specific, and doable.
    whenLabel: WHEN WILL YOU DO IT?
    whenChoices:
    - Today
    - Tomorrow
    - This week
    closeCaseButton: Close the case
    resultHeading: Case dismissed
    starsFormat: '{n} of 3 stars'
    caseFileFormat: 'THE WORRY ON TRIAL

      "{worry}"


      THE BALANCED THOUGHT

      {balanced}


      THE
      PLAN

      {plan} ({when})'
    trapsHeading: THINKING TRAPS SPOTTED
    trapLineFormat: '- {trap}: {description}'
    strikesLabel: 'GAVEL STRIKES:'
    nextCaseButton: Next case
    replayButton: Replay this case
    continueButton: Continue
    exitButton: Exit
    closeEarlyButton: Close
    doneMark: ' (Done)'
    recessHeading: Recess
    recessBody: Three gavel strikes. The judge calls a short break. Breathe in for
      four counts and out for six, then come back. The helpful answers will be outlined
      from now on.
    recessButton: Back to court
